## Report
Validated the finding on commit 5e7f1f0fab7193b05a0927419f76d4209279ac98. Code inspection showed that the commit changed role dispatch so Frontend and Combined now enter run_remote_frontend (crates/argmin-s3/src/main.rs:134-142), whereas the previous commit exited as unsupported for remote frontend roles. run_remote_frontend calls run_frontend_server(..., false) (crates/argmin-s3/src/main.rs:255-262). That false selects Coordinator::new_with_managed_key_provider_for_storage_cluster_without_background_sweepers (crates/argmin-s3/src/main.rs:329-343), whose constructor passes false and disabled lifecycle/scavenger sweepers (crates/server-core/src/coordinator/infra.rs:288-305). infra.rs:404-410 uses that false to create ReclaimSweeper::disabled instead of ReclaimSweeper::spawn. The spawned reclaim worker is the only observed consumer of wait_for_reclaim_work that calls try_reclaim_object_payload_for and try_finalize_bucket_delete_for (crates/server-core/src/coordinator/runtime.rs:83-105); grep of argmin-s3/storage-node RPC/server files found no replacement consumer. Delete/overwrite/bucket-delete paths enqueue reclaim work at delete.rs:114-118, put.rs:280-285, and bucket.rs:368-370. I then added a targeted unit PoC using the same no-background-sweeper constructor used by the remote frontend path. It creates a bucket, puts an object, deletes it as an authenticated requester, then checks the underlying StorageCluster reclaim queue. The PoC observed storage::ReclaimWorkItem::ObjectPayload for bucket/key and intentionally panicked with 'queued reclaim work remained undrained after authenticated delete'. This demonstrates metadata-visible deletion while physical reclaim work remains queued with no background worker to drain it. cargo test produced a failing/panicking PoC. Valgrind was attempted but not installed. LLDB was run non-interactively with a breakpoint on rust_begin_unwind and captured the PoC panic backtrace at core_tests.rs:7933.

