## Narrative
The finding is real and reachable in the newly enabled remote frontend/combined runtime path. main.rs dispatches Frontend and Combined into run_remote_frontend, and run_remote_frontend calls run_frontend_server with false for start_background_sweepers. run_frontend_server then constructs the coordinator with the without_background_sweepers constructor. That constructor explicitly passes false for the reclaim worker and disabled lifecycle/scavenger factories; infra.rs uses false to create ReclaimSweeper::disabled instead of spawning the argmin-reclaim thread. The spawned thread is the code that consumes wait_for_reclaim_work and invokes try_reclaim_object_payload_for and try_finalize_bucket_delete_for. Meanwhile normal delete, overwrite, and bucket-delete operations enqueue reclaim/finalization work. An authenticated client can therefore cause old payloads and delete-finalization work to accumulate until storage is exhausted. Severity remains medium: the impact is high availability loss, but it requires a specific process role, reachable deployment, and valid S3 write/delete authorization, with no confidentiality or integrity bypass shown.
## Controls
- SigV4 authentication through authenticate_request
- Coordinator authorization for object and bucket operations
- Default listener is 127.0.0.1:9000 unless ARGMIN_LISTEN_ADDR is changed
- Remote frontend/combined roles require a complete ARGMIN_STORAGE_NODE_SOCKETS map
- TLS is optional only when ARGMIN_TLS_CERT_PATH and ARGMIN_TLS_KEY_PATH are configured
- Connection and in-flight request limits exist, but no repository evidence of disk quotas or reclaim backlog limits
## Blindspots
- Static repository artifacts do not include Kubernetes, cloud, load balancer, or production deployment manifests, so public exposure cannot be proven.
- This attack-path stage did not run a full HTTP end-to-end exploit; it relies on static reachability plus earlier executable validation at the coordinator/storage level.
- Operational controls such as external quotas, disk monitoring, or out-of-band cleanup jobs may exist outside the repository and could reduce practical impact.
- README text appears stale about frontend/combined support, but code and the Phase 10.5 plan text show the roles are now runnable.
